<p>Israel said early Saturday that its military had begun striking what it called Hezbollah infrastructure in Beirut, as local media and reporters described two loud explosions and smoke over the Lebanese capital&#x27;s southern suburbs. The strikes came after Israeli action against a bridge in eastern Lebanon that, Israel said, it destroyed to stop Hezbollah reinforcements from crossing. Le Monde reported that Lebanese authorities said Israeli warplanes destroyed the bridge and killed civilians leaving a mosque, highlighting the immediate human toll alongside the military escalation. The new strikes add to recent Israeli attacks on Beirut&#x27;s southern suburbs as the conflict spreads across multiple fronts. Al-Monitor also reported missiles fired toward Israel from Iran and an Israeli air-defense response that left one person wounded, according to medics.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/HFEr_EQr0S8Zl8xeqN6QtdlHAczdlvR2APMaACDf-nHDauRYoZdFIiSR7RwwhFEyxqUQ_s4TXy-ZxIopPba-r63XKcvb47YIRc7iHTE3NcTJXJGqg8sT-7rkrWecyROlInsohVjetKN5qFLYOAMYpITwm5RQRaDfzGKFZvdZSoL7qsucqA' alt='A photograph shows a collapsed building at the site of an overnight Israeli airstrike in the Haret Hreik neighborhood of Beirut’s southern suburbs on April 3, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Where it hit: Local media said the latest strike zone was Beirut&#x27;s southern suburbs, an area hit repeatedly in recent days.</li><li>Israel&#x27;s stated aim: Israel said it struck the bridge to block Hezbollah movement and reinforcements between areas in eastern Lebanon.</li><li>Wider regional fallout: The same round of developments included missiles fired toward Israel from Iran, with Israeli air defenses activated and medics reporting one person wounded.</li></ul><blockquote>Hezbollah infrastructure - Israeli military</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Israeli military: The military said it had begun striking sites it identified as Hezbollah infrastructure in Beirut and that it de